# Llama 3 8B on a node of 8 GPUs, as Megatron-Bridge's B300 recipe trains it: a global
# batch of 128 rows of 8192 in microbatches of 4 rows a GPU, in MXFP8. Megatron
# publishes no B300 number for it; on 8 B200s, whose dense FP8 peak is a B300's, it
# trains at 29,521 tokens a second a GPU in MXFP8 (25.11). Its parameters split by FSDP,
# or only its optimizer's state, as Megatron's distributed optimizer splits it.
#
#   python scripts/benchmark.py run examples/benchmarks/megatron_llama3_8b.bux --out new.json
use llama3_8b

mesh    = mesh(fsdp=8)
layout  = fsdp: layout | zero1: layout(zero=1)
methods = methods(microbatches=4)

data      = synthetic
optimizer = adamw(lr=3e-4)
seq_len   = 8192
batch     = 128
steps     = 12
log       = log(every=3)
precision = precision(compute=bfloat16, matmuls=mxfp8)
